\description{
Fits a partially confirmatory multiple-indicators multiple-causes (MIMIC)
model by a variational Bayes EM algorithm, with continuous spike-and-slab
regularization on \strong{both} the measurement and the structural part. Items
load on factors through a measurement design matrix \code{Q_A}, while covariates
predict the factors through a structural design matrix \code{Q_B}; entries of
either that are left unspecified are selected from the data.
}
\details{
This is the MIMIC member of the \code{vbpm} family and is the companion of
\code{\link[=vbfa]{vbfa()}}, which fits the measurement part alone. The two share the \code{-1/0/1}
design-matrix convention and the spike-and-slab formulation.
}
\note{
The evidence lower bound is \strong{not} currently returned. The published
algorithm converges on the weighted residual vector rather than on the
bound, and the bound's implementable closed form has not been assembled.
\code{\link[=fit_stats]{fit_stats()}} does accept a \code{vbmimic} fit, but returns a deliberately
limited result: \code{n_active_coef} (soft-selected measurement and structural
coefficients) plus typed \code{NA} for every covariance-based index and
parameter count, with an explanatory \code{note} attribute. \code{\link[=pefa]{pefa()}} does not
accept \code{vbmimic} fits at all, because factor-number selection needs a
comparable objective.
}
\examples{
## 3 factors, 18 items, 9 covariates in disjoint blocks of 3
B <- matrix(0, 3, 9)
for (k in 1:3) B[k, ((k - 1) * 3 + 1):(k * 3)] <- .3
sim <- sim_lvm(N = 300, K = 3, J = 18, P = 9, b = B, phx = 0, rseed = 1)
Y <- sim$dat[, 1:18]
X <- sim$dat[, 19:27]

## two anchored items per factor; the structural part left exploratory.
## Anchoring at least one part is advisable: with both Q_A and Q_B fully
## exploratory the solution can be rotationally ambiguous.
Q_A <- matrix(-1L, 18, 3)
for (k in 1:3) {
  a <- which(rep(1:3, each = 6) == k)[1:2]
  Q_A[a, ] <- 0L; Q_A[a, k] <- 1L
}
Q_B <- matrix(-1L, 3, 9)

fit <- vbmimic(Y, X, Q_A, Q_B)
fit$flag           # 1 if converged
round(fit$B, 2)    # structural coefficients

}
